  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "COMBIN and COMBINA return 83.99999999999999 (1 ULP below 84) for C(9, 3) via cyclic x87-stored factors with * n last",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20228, COMBIN(n, k) truncates n and k (with subnormals treated as signed zero and n <= 2,147,483,646), reduces k = min(k, n - k), and evaluates product(i=2..=k, (n-k+i-1)/i) * n, storing every division and accumulator product from x87 PC64 to binary64 and multiplying n last. Because 7/2 * 8/3 * 9 divides by 3 before multiplying by 9, COMBIN(9, 3) and COMBINA(7, 3) return 83.99999999999999 (0x4054ffffffffffff) instead of exact 84 (0x4055000000000000). COMBINA truncates its two arguments independently before forming total = trunc(n) + trunc(k) - 1 and evaluates trunc(n) == 0 && trunc(k) == 0 -> 1 before checking negative k, so COMBINA(-0.25, 0.75) returns 1.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 20,713 COMBIN discovery rows, 1,024 cyclic held-out rows, and 35,233 COMBINA identity rows in Excel 16.0 build 20228 (CalcFunc-Evidence work/w109/G4-04-combin/ and G4-04-combina/), and matched on 25,199/25,199 COMBIN and 40,991/40,991 COMBINA full-bank rows.",
